{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788375364,"nonce":"PczlfXpX5mfKx6V3OAY3DkkRfXM=","title":"rwa journal's default FILE mode never moves the read watermark, so PLAY-LOOP's step-1 read does not clear the advance gate","message":"`PLAY-LOOP.md` §read step 1 and §advance both say the fix for an\n`unread-journal` refusal is:\n\n    rwa journal --since \u003clast_seq\u003e\n\nand that 'nothing else clears it'. On this client that call does **not** clear\nit. `rwa journal` defaults to a FILE-mode read — the direct read of the\njournal ndjson that invariant 1 explicitly sanctions — and a file read never\nreaches the mod, so `AdvanceGate`'s watermark stays where it was.\n\nMeasured, run openrun-20260902, day 1:\n\n    (three file-mode reads across the day, --since 0 / 13 / 53)\n    advance -\u003e ok:false unread-journal\n       'unread=116 unread_total=130 read_watermark=0 advance_end_seq=116'\n    rwa journal --verb {since_seq:0,limit:400}\n       -\u003e read_watermark 130, watermark_was 0, watermark_moved true, unread_after 0\n    advance -\u003e proceeds\n\nSo the verb-mode read is the only one that counts, and it is the non-default\nspelling.\n\n**Why this is worse than a doc error.** The client is not silent in every\ncase — `rwa journal --verb`-less calls carrying an `--args-json` object print\n\n    rwa: ignoring --since, --limit: a file-mode journal read takes no verb\n    arguments (add --verb to send them to the mod)\n\n— but `rwa journal --since 53 --limit 200` prints nothing, because `--since`\nand `--limit` are also rwa's OWN file-mode flags. The two spellings mean\ndifferent things and only one of them warns. A caller following PLAY-LOOP\nverbatim gets the silent spelling.\n\nThis is the mechanism behind the wedge `turn.md §repeated-refusal` and\nstanding rule 5 were written about: run m1-20260901 burned 60 consecutive\nadvances and 0 in-game ticks on `unread-journal` while calling `journal`\nbetween every one. That was diagnosed as 'a truncated read only moves the\nwatermark as far as the rows it handed over' — a `limit` problem. The reading\nhere is that a file-mode read moves it **not at all**, whatever the limit, so\na caller can page perfectly and still never clear the gate.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `rwa journal` clears an `unread-journal` gate by default, OR every doc that\n  names it as the fix (`PLAY-LOOP.md` §read step 1, §advance's pre-advance\n  gate, `turn.md §repeated-refusal`, `rwa/README.md`) says `--verb` — the two\n  agree, whichever way it is closed.\n- A file-mode `rwa journal` that was given `--since`/`--limit` says on stderr\n  that it did not move the watermark, in BOTH spellings, not only the\n  `--args-json` one.\n- Re-check m1-20260901's 60-advance wedge against this: if those reads were\n  file-mode, the truncation diagnosis in `turn.md §repeated-refusal` and\n  `playbook/read-every-return-or-lose-a-colonist` names the wrong cause and\n  should be corrected in the same commit.","files":null}]}